(a) The chief of police of the City of West Point, or his or her designee (such designee specifically to include, but not be limited to the animal control officer), is hereby designated as the person responsible for determining when:
(1) A dog is a potentially vicious animal;
(2) A dog is a vicious animal;
(3) When a dog is a nuisance;
(4) A domestic animal is a stray animal;
(5) A domestic animal is an injured animal;
(6) Any animal's behavior or condition is in violation of any provision of this article; or
(7) When any owner, keeper, custodian or responsible person for an animal is in violation of this article.
(b) Any determination by the chief of police, or his or her designee, of any of the conditions or violations set forth above which will or may result in the destruction or euthanasia of the animal, shall, when feasible or possible, be communicated to the owner, keeper, or custodian of the animal.
(c) An appeal of the determination of the chief of police, or his or her designee, shall be to the animal control board. Such appeal must be in writing and must be received by the city clerk within two (2) business days of receipt by the owner, keeper, or custodian of the determination by the chief of police, or his or her designee.
(d) The animal control board shall schedule an appeal proceeding to hear the evidence with regard to the determination made by the chief of police, or his or her designee, and to decide the legitimacy of that determination. Such appeal shall be heard within ten (10) business days of the receipt of such written appeal. The animal control board shall adopt, reject, or modify, in its discretion, the determination of the chief of police, or his or her designee. Such decision of the animal control board shall be final.
(e) Any person eligible to file an appeal hereunder may sign a waiver of appeal if so desired. In such case, if euthanasia would be the final result of the determination by the chief of police, or his or her designee, the animal may be euthanized and no additional costs will accrue to the owner, keeper, or custodian.
(Ord. No. 2010-08, § 1(Exh. A), 8-9-10)

